NCCL source
-----------
nccl/ holds NVIDIA NCCL's network-plugin headers, copied unchanged (byte-identical) from NVIDIA NCCL tag
v2.32.3-1, plugins/net/example/nccl/: common.h, err.h, gin_v11.h, net.h, net_device.h, net_v2.h, net_v3.h,
net_v4.h, net_v5.h, net_v6.h, net_v7.h, net_v8.h, net_v9.h, net_v10.h, net_v11.h, net_v12.h and types.h.
Copyright (c) 2017-2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved. They are licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0; NCCL's licence text is in nccl/LICENSE.txt.

No NCCL source is copied into net_sircl.c. These NCCL v2.32.3-1 sources were read for NCCL's behaviour and not
adapted: src/transport/net_ib/connect.cc, p2p.cc, init.cc, reg.cc and gdr.cc; src/transport/net.cc;
src/graph/topo.cc; src/init.cc.

SIRCL and RoCEnante
-------------------
net-sircl follows the transport design of SparkRing's SIRCL ring sessions (sparkring-sircl), which derive from
RoCEnante, the b12x one-shot RoCE collectives (b12x/comm/roce), by Local Inference Lab
(https://github.com/local-inference-lab) and its contributors, including Luke Alonso (lukealonso), licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. RoCEnante was written by Jason (original-el8) in
local-inference-lab/b12x PR 295, with dual-rail striping and graph-collective work by Luke Alonso
(lukealonso). b12x is developed inside FlashInfer at flashinfer/experimental/b12x.

What net-sircl takes from that design: one-sided RDMA writes ordered on one queue pair and closed by 4-byte
flag words; the use of both PCI functions of a cable as two lanes (dual rail); and a cap on the bytes in
flight toward a peer reached through relays. Its route derivation follows SIRCL's route planner
(sparkring_sircl/routes.py, derive_lanes), written again in C. No RoCEnante or SIRCL source file is copied
into net_sircl.c.

Test infrastructure
-------------------
tests/standin/ contains compatibility includes into transport-core, which owns
SparkRing's shared-memory verbs provider. Retain transport-core/LICENSE,
transport-core/NOTICE and transport-core/PROVENANCE.json in a standalone package.
The provider is test infrastructure and is not linked into the real-NIC plugin.

Shared transport extraction
---------------------------
Device metadata, topology derivation, RC queue-pair setup, registration,
posting/completion primitives and window arithmetic use transport-core 0.1.0.
The ext-net API, CTS protocol, registration policy and progress scheduling remain
owned by net-sircl. Hardware measurements for the shared-core source a4de4dd5 are summarized in
../docs/measurements.md, with scope and conditions. They are not performance guarantees.
